course: dictionary
lesson: 4689
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and homer is one of them. It can be a home run in baseball, a name, a pigeon, or even a sports decision. You must look at the words around it to know which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Homer's poems tell of the Greeks besieging Troy for ten years and of the hero Odysseus's long journey home.» The clues are poems and a hero's long journey. Homer here is a person who wrote poems, so it is a name, not a home run.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Put your meaning in place of the word and read it again. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well.
fact: Homer can mean a home run in baseball, when a batter runs all the way round the bases and scores.
fact: Homer is also a name: Homer was an ancient Greek poet who is said to have composed the «Iliad» and the «Odyssey».
fact: Homer Simpson is the dad in the cartoon «The Simpsons», and he often says «D'oh!».
fact: A homer can also be a homing pigeon, a bird that finds its way back home.
fact: The word «legend» means a old story that may not be true, such as the wooden horse of Troy.
exercise: Fans in the USA say «hit a homer». What does it mean? | A cartoon dad who says D'oh | A pigeon that flies home | A hit that lands in the sea | *A home run, scoring all the way round the bases
exercise: «Homer's poems tell of the Greeks besieging Troy.» Which meaning of Homer fits this sentence? | A referee who favours the home team | *A name for an ancient Greek poet | A homing pigeon | A home run in baseball
exercise: Who is Homer Simpson? | A homing pigeon | An ancient Greek poet | *The dad in the cartoon «The Simpsons» | The hero of the «Odyssey»
test: Ask: which meaning fits? «The homer was a decision that seemed to favour the home team.» What does homer mean? | A home run in baseball | A bird that flies home | *A referee's decision that seems to favour the home team | A name for a Greek poet
test: «The wooden horse is a story from legend, not proven history.» What does legend mean here? | A type of bird | A map | *An old story that may not be true | A famous person
exam: «Homer's poems tell of the Greeks besieging Troy for ten years; no one is sure Homer was one real person.» Which meaning of homer fits best, and how do the clues show it? | A home run, because the Greeks were batters | A referee, because the Greeks won the game | A homing pigeon, because the poems fly home | *A name for the ancient poet, because of the poems and Troy
